# Git and Commit Rules

Use conventional commits.

Examples:
- feat: add tenant module
- fix: resolve refresh token rotation
- refactor: clean auth service
- chore: update eslint config
- test: add permission guard tests

Before commit:
- run lint
- run type-check
- run tests if available
- ensure no secrets are committed
- ensure .env files are ignored

Never commit:
- .env
- private keys
- database dumps
- access tokens
- refresh tokens
- API secrets
